(2678829, 368141, 45533, '<td valign="top">It''s a great photo--but I have one suggestion; when it''s advanced editing, clone out the spots of you in the reflection of the flass on the black squares.<br/> <br/>Despite that, it will probably place high.  At least, that''s my prediction.</td>', 'It''s a great photo--but I have one suggestion; when it''s advanced editing, clone out the spots of you in the reflection of the flass on the black squares. Despite that, it will probably place high.  At least, that''s my prediction.', '2006-07-31 07:28:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2678847, 369649, 45533, '<td valign="top">Damn these Iceland-ic photographers...they''re all too good!<br/> <br/>Anyway, this is has a definite "WOW" factor.  It almost makes you wonder if it is truly black and white, but you know it''s not by the hints of blue.<br/> <br/>Absolutely stunning, I give this a 9.</td>', 'Damn these Iceland-ic photographers...they''re all too good! Anyway, this is has a definite "WOW" factor.  It almost makes you wonder if it is truly black and white, but you know it''s not by the hints of blue. Absolutely stunning, I give this a 9.', '2006-07-31 07:34:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2678856, 367684, 45533, '<td valign="top">Okay, I''ll be perfectly honest.  In the thumbnail, it looked very "wow", but then on the large version, not so good.  The lines weren''t even trying to be straight, and I usually think on this type of photo, they need to be.  I see how maybe (and this is just my guess), that you thought that the checkers should be askew because of the stem of the glass not being straight.  I personally think one or the other is enough--you don''t need both to be not straight on a type of photo like this.<br/> <br/>I give this a 6.</td>', 'Okay, I''ll be perfectly honest.  In the thumbnail, it looked very "wow", but then on the large version, not so good.  The lines weren''t even trying to be straight, and I usually think on this type of photo, they need to be.  I see how maybe (and this is just my guess), that you thought that the checkers should be askew because of the stem of the glass not being straight.  I personally think one or the other is enough--you don''t need both to be not straight on a type of photo like this. I give this a 6.', '2006-07-31 07:37:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2678874, 369333, 45533, '<td valign="top">Metiulously (too lazy to look up the correct spelling) done.  It''s a really great graphical work.  The exactness of how far the glasses on either side of the spilt one, how full they are, etc.<br/> <br/>The only problems with this image are these:<br/>Personally, I would like the spilt one to be a little more exactly split in the middle of the backgrounds.  Not easy to do, just a little nitpicky thing I have.<br/>And the lighting/reflections.  I''ve done shots of glasses before, or at least attempted to, and I know that this, too, is in no way easy.  The one on the right looks a bit better than the one on the left, just because of the background being white.<br/> <br/>Oh, and the glass in the middle?  Try spot shining the black side of the bottom of the glass, it would make it look a little cleaner.<br/> <br/>Overall?  I give this a 7.  I may change it to an 8 later today, I''m sort of on the fence.</td>', 'Metiulously (too lazy to look up the correct spelling) done.  It''s a really great graphical work.  The exactness of how far the glasses on either side of the spilt one, how full they are, etc. The only problems with this image are these:Personally, I would like the spilt one to be a little more exactly split in the middle of the backgrounds.  Not easy to do, just a little nitpicky thing I have.And the lighting/reflections.  I''ve done shots of glasses before, or at least attempted to, and I know that this, too, is in no way easy.  The one on the right looks a bit better than the one on the left, just because of the background being white. Oh, and the glass in the middle?  Try spot shining the black side of the bottom of the glass, it would make it look a little cleaner. Overall?  I give this a 7.  I may change it to an 8 later today, I''m sort of on the fence.', '2006-07-31 07:41:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2678883, 369892, 45533, '<td valign="top">Another one that looks a bit better in the thumbnail.  It''s just not very cleanly done.  I know it''s not the easiest thing in the world to do, too, but it could have been made a little better with spot editing.  Just things like the split between the two backgrounds, and the blue halo around the white side of the glass.<br/> <br/>Overall, I give this a 6.  Good effort.  :)</td>', 'Another one that looks a bit better in the thumbnail.  It''s just not very cleanly done.  I know it''s not the easiest thing in the world to do, too, but it could have been made a little better with spot editing.  Just things like the split between the two backgrounds, and the blue halo around the white side of the glass. Overall, I give this a 6.  Good effort.  :)', '2006-07-31 07:45:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2678899, 369467, 45533, '<td valign="top">I have 3 complaints about this image, which could have been made better with just a little better post-processing.<br/> <br/>1.) Noise.  That pretty much speaks for itself.<br/>2.) Border.  The white of the border makes the background look incredibly cyan.<br/>3.) Size of the image.  The maximum size of an image on DPC is 640x640.  Use that to your advantage.<br/> <br/>Without those post-processing flaws, I tell you, that it could have been a 8 or a 9.  It''s a great graphical work, with great composition.<br/> <br/>But, alas, I give it a 6.</td>', 'I have 3 complaints about this image, which could have been made better with just a little better post-processing. 1.) Noise.  That pretty much speaks for itself.2.) Border.  The white of the border makes the background look incredibly cyan.3.) Size of the image.  The maximum size of an image on DPC is 640x640.  Use that to your advantage. Without those post-processing flaws, I tell you, that it could have been a 8 or a 9.  It''s a great graphical work, with great composition. But, alas, I give it a 6.', '2006-07-31 07:49:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2678911, 369029, 45533, '<td valign="top">I love this picture almost as I love Oreos.<br/> <br/>But it could be better in two ways.  One, backdrop.  I''m guessing you used a white bedsheet?  The wrinkles near the back are distracting.  Second, just a little flaw, a light reflection in the handle of the cup.  :)<br/> <br/>I still give it a 6, plus one for the fact that you made me want Oreos and milk.</td>', 'I love this picture almost as I love Oreos. But it could be better in two ways.  One, backdrop.  I''m guessing you used a white bedsheet?  The wrinkles near the back are distracting.  Second, just a little flaw, a light reflection in the handle of the cup.  :) I still give it a 6, plus one for the fact that you made me want Oreos and milk.', '2006-07-31 07:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
