(2686227, 367804, 36988, '<td valign="top">Outstanding job! Congratulations on a great finish... :)</td>', 'Outstanding job! Congratulations on a great finish... :)', '2006-08-02 01:39:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686233, 369838, 36988, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done. Great finish... :)</td>', 'Beautifully done. Great finish... :)', '2006-08-02 01:40:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686234, 367804, 41802, '<td valign="top">Wow and congrats, this was my favorite.  You did an exception job with the topic!</td>', 'Wow and congrats, this was my favorite.  You did an exception job with the topic!', '2006-08-02 01:40:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686236, 368529, 15358, '<td valign="top">Congratulations to the photo above mine.  I really like the image.  His right foot is a tad out of focus... since he was moving but it is the only thing that detracts from a very nice image.  Good luck on future challenges.</td>', 'Congratulations to the photo above mine.  I really like the image.  His right foot is a tad out of focus... since he was moving but it is the only thing that detracts from a very nice image.  Good luck on future challenges.', '2006-08-02 01:40:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686243, 369649, 36988, '<td valign="top">Beautifully captured with a very ethereal feel... congratulations!</td>', 'Beautifully captured with a very ethereal feel... congratulations!', '2006-08-02 01:41:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686244, 369706, 61930, '<td valign="top">This was my first ever entry, and I am a newbie to this in general and thought I''d give it a try.  I didn''t realize the rules - but as soon as the voting began, and I saw all the other awesome shots I did a lovely hand-to-the-forehead "d''oh".  That''s ok, I enjoyed it and have already submitted again - you can only learn (and read the rules better.)  Thank you for the comments everybody. :-)</td>', 'This was my first ever entry, and I am a newbie to this in general and thought I''d give it a try.  I didn''t realize the rules - but as soon as the voting began, and I saw all the other awesome shots I did a lovely hand-to-the-forehead "d''oh".  That''s ok, I enjoyed it and have already submitted again - you can only learn (and read the rules better.)  Thank you for the comments everybody. :-)', '2006-08-02 01:41:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686259, 369742, 20168, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your "brown" ribbon, an esteemed honor among the DPC community!</td>', 'Congrats on your "brown" ribbon, an esteemed honor among the DPC community!', '2006-08-02 01:42:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686265, 367804, 41337, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon! Great image.</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon! Great image.', '2006-08-02 01:43:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686287, 369428, 57278, '<td valign="top">weel done, congrats on your top ten finish. (looks a little Zenish if you know what i mean)</td>', 'weel done, congrats on your top ten finish. (looks a little Zenish if you know what i mean)', '2006-08-02 01:46:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686305, 367804, 31133, '<td valign="top">WOW! First ribbon ever and it''s a blue!! Congratulations. It must feel soooo good to look at your entry all week on the front page. WTG!</td>', 'WOW! First ribbon ever and it''s a blue!! Congratulations. It must feel soooo good to look at your entry all week on the front page. WTG!', '2006-08-02 01:49:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686310, 369825, 40718, '<td valign="top">I think you did fairly well here with a 5.5.  A few thoughts:<br/> <br/>1) The black arrowhead blends too much with the black rocks of the background.  It also has that funny reflection down the middle.<br/>2) The composition is very centered.  That doesn''t give us any dynamism in the shot which is already static being basically a still life of small objects.<br/>3) The white arrowhead is almost blown out.<br/> <br/>Keep working at it.  5.5 isn''t a bad score at all on this site.  I see you''ve done better, but we can''t win em all, eh?</td>', 'I think you did fairly well here with a 5.5.  A few thoughts: 1) The black arrowhead blends too much with the black rocks of the background.  It also has that funny reflection down the middle.2) The composition is very centered.  That doesn''t give us any dynamism in the shot which is already static being basically a still life of small objects.3) The white arrowhead is almost blown out. Keep working at it.  5.5 isn''t a bad score at all on this site.  I see you''ve done better, but we can''t win em all, eh?', '2006-08-02 01:49:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686318, 367804, 52467, '<td valign="top">Way to go Crystal!</td>', 'Way to go Crystal!', '2006-08-02 01:51:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686355, 368977, 49643, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your nice comments &amp; appreciating the photo. Well I will like to describe the idea behind the photo. The King who had lost his war &amp; a dead pawn near his feat.The dead pawn, the light, exposure &amp; long shadows were used to create the atmosphere of defeat, sadness. The standing King shows his character such as confidence as well as courage.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-28 01:14:50.</i></td>', 'Thanks for your nice comments & appreciating the photo. Well I will like to describe the idea behind the photo. The King who had lost his war & a dead pawn near his feat.The dead pawn, the light, exposure & long shadows were used to create the atmosphere of defeat, sadness. The standing King shows his character such as confidence as well as courage.', '2006-08-02 01:57:27.000000', '2008-07-28 02:14:50.000000', 0),
(2686390, 367259, 40718, '<td valign="top">Another 5.5 for me to critique.  I could tell this would be at the top of the range as it has some dynamics to it, even though it''s a fairly simple image.  The best part is the diagonal composition you chose and the shallow DOF which puts the 3 OOF.  Excellent stuff.<br/> <br/>Would I change anything?  Totally minor, but I may have moved the chalk just a bit to the left so it doesn''t interfere with the 1.  Other than that, I think you did about as well with the image as you could.  The only problem is it''s general lack of "wow".  On DPC "wow" gets you to the higher scores.  You can see this by the vast majority of votes being 5 or 6.  People give those votes to picture which are technically well done but don''t quite hold their attention long enough to get higher.</td>', 'Another 5.5 for me to critique.  I could tell this would be at the top of the range as it has some dynamics to it, even though it''s a fairly simple image.  The best part is the diagonal composition you chose and the shallow DOF which puts the 3 OOF.  Excellent stuff. Would I change anything?  Totally minor, but I may have moved the chalk just a bit to the left so it doesn''t interfere with the 1.  Other than that, I think you did about as well with the image as you could.  The only problem is it''s general lack of "wow".  On DPC "wow" gets you to the higher scores.  You can see this by the vast majority of votes being 5 or 6.  People give those votes to picture which are technically well done but don''t quite hold their attention long enough to get higher.', '2006-08-02 02:02:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686391, 368338, 41899, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  I gave you a 10 but forgot to tell you earlier how much I liked this photo.</td>', 'Congratulations!  I gave you a 10 but forgot to tell you earlier how much I liked this photo.', '2006-08-02 02:02:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686412, 369338, 41899, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  I really like the textures in this.  Sorry I didn''t write sooner but I did give this a 9.</td>', 'Congratulations!  I really like the textures in this.  Sorry I didn''t write sooner but I did give this a 9.', '2006-08-02 02:05:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686414, 369296, 40718, '<td valign="top">I haven''t looked at the comments, but I bet a large part of your problem was meeting the challenge.  For a picture that is supposed to be B&amp;W, there is an awful lot of yellow in those rings.<br/> <br/>The idea is creative and I like that.  The picture is very centered which leads to a static feel.  Also, the DOF doesn''t help us. I would have increased it enough to make the whole ring in focus rather than having the back portion OOF.  Or, if you wanted a shallow DOF, I would have focused on the back portion rather than the front because it stands out more than the front which gets a bit lost in the foil.</td>', 'I haven''t looked at the comments, but I bet a large part of your problem was meeting the challenge.  For a picture that is supposed to be B&W, there is an awful lot of yellow in those rings. The idea is creative and I like that.  The picture is very centered which leads to a static feel.  Also, the DOF doesn''t help us. I would have increased it enough to make the whole ring in focus rather than having the back portion OOF.  Or, if you wanted a shallow DOF, I would have focused on the back portion rather than the front because it stands out more than the front which gets a bit lost in the foil.', '2006-08-02 02:06:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686437, 369296, 48541, '<td valign="top">The photo is well composed but there is too much going on for me.  It is a little hard to look and take in.</td>', 'The photo is well composed but there is too much going on for me.  It is a little hard to look and take in.', '2006-08-02 02:09:20.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2686452, 369838, 19978, '<td valign="top">Brilliantly done!</td>', 'Brilliantly done!', '2006-08-02 02:11:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686483, 369838, 40718, '<td valign="top">well done techo.  I''ve always wanted to do this iconic shot.</td>', 'well done techo.  I''ve always wanted to do this iconic shot.', '2006-08-02 02:14:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686541, 369744, 47852, '<td valign="top">Loved this one!  Thanks for taking the time to jot down the notes on how this was achieved!  :)</td>', 'Loved this one!  Thanks for taking the time to jot down the notes on how this was achieved!  :)', '2006-08-02 02:25:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686570, 368272, 47852, '<td valign="top">Going back through the images from this challenge, I found this one to be underrated as far as my voting.  I thought the creative use of light and shadows was fantastic with the unique shape of the objects.  I can see the voters points though about cleaning things up a bit before shooting.  Either way, I think this shot should have scored higher.  Keep up the great work!</td>', 'Going back through the images from this challenge, I found this one to be underrated as far as my voting.  I thought the creative use of light and shadows was fantastic with the unique shape of the objects.  I can see the voters points though about cleaning things up a bit before shooting.  Either way, I think this shot should have scored higher.  Keep up the great work!', '2006-08-02 02:30:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686581, 367804, 60899, '<td valign="top">And so ends the long jittery week....congrats on the much deserved win.....:)</td>', 'And so ends the long jittery week....congrats on the much deserved win.....:)', '2006-08-02 02:32:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686655, 367804, 34938, '<td valign="top">I knew you would get the blue by your discussions on the forums Crystal....YAY!!!! This deserved the ribbon and it''s one of the most creative shots I have seen on this site...this will take you to another level and you will go from strength to strength...this is high class stuff...may you get many, many more of these elusive ribbons</td>', 'I knew you would get the blue by your discussions on the forums Crystal....YAY!!!! This deserved the ribbon and it''s one of the most creative shots I have seen on this site...this will take you to another level and you will go from strength to strength...this is high class stuff...may you get many, many more of these elusive ribbons', '2006-08-02 02:47:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686666, 369570, 60899, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> The contrast here is pretty low.  Also, the paper''s color is waaaay off-white.  Perhaps different lighting would''ve made it brighter? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Loved the paper color.....gives an antique touch.....Definately should have been in top 20.....</td>', 'Originally posted by levyj413: The contrast here is pretty low.  Also, the paper''s color is waaaay off-white.  Perhaps different lighting would''ve made it brighter?   Loved the paper color.....gives an antique touch.....Definately should have been in top 20.....', '2006-08-02 02:48:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686685, 367804, 16230, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first ribbon Crystal, and a very interesting image. Well done!</td>', 'Congratulations on your first ribbon Crystal, and a very interesting image. Well done!', '2006-08-02 02:51:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686686, 369649, 31443, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! Fantastic rendering of colored b/w<br/>Til hamingju! Það er aldeilis hraðferðin hjá þér að sanka að þér borðum, gaman að þessu :) kominn með þrjár á Nikon D50 hæst metnu myndirnar</td>', 'Congratulations! Fantastic rendering of colored b/wTil hamingju! Það er aldeilis hraðferðin hjá þér að sanka að þér borðum, gaman að þessu :) kominn með þrjár á Nikon D50 hæst metnu myndirnar', '2006-08-02 02:51:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686695, 369838, 34938, '<td valign="top">hopefully you''ll get to keep this ribbon! excellent shot...I love the title</td>', 'hopefully you''ll get to keep this ribbon! excellent shot...I love the title', '2006-08-02 02:52:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686706, 369277, 30214, '<td valign="top">Great shot, Neil! Congratulations! <br/> <br/>(i need a wide angle lens... i need a wide angle lens... I need a...)</td>', 'Great shot, Neil! Congratulations!  (i need a wide angle lens... i need a wide angle lens... I need a...)', '2006-08-02 02:54:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686708, 369649, 34938, '<td valign="top">Now you have the ribbon set Magnús! Well done and another, I mean YET ANOTHER ribbon for Iceland...you guys are the best!</td>', 'Now you have the ribbon set Magnús! Well done and another, I mean YET ANOTHER ribbon for Iceland...you guys are the best!', '2006-08-02 02:54:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686709, 369078, 31443, '<td valign="top">Wonderful capture! Thought this was in Iceland! Congratulations on top 10, favorite for sure..</td>', 'Wonderful capture! Thought this was in Iceland! Congratulations on top 10, favorite for sure..', '2006-08-02 02:54:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686730, 369078, 49865, '<td valign="top">This remains one of my favorites from the challenge. There is so much energy radiating from, the, er, Angler.</td>', 'This remains one of my favorites from the challenge. There is so much energy radiating from, the, er, Angler.', '2006-08-02 02:58:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686748, 369742, 6498, '<td valign="top">Remember, keep practicing..and I''ll bet..you will get better...My Wife and I have had a brown ribbon..  <br/> <br/>Tom and Sandi Farrell</td>', 'Remember, keep practicing..and I''ll bet..you will get better...My Wife and I have had a brown ribbon..   Tom and Sandi Farrell', '2006-08-02 03:03:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686768, 369742, 6498, '<td valign="top">Sorry...Tom was on my site again looking at my placing.  I do agree with what he said though...don''t give up, keep trying.</td>', 'Sorry...Tom was on my site again looking at my placing.  I do agree with what he said though...don''t give up, keep trying.', '2006-08-02 03:09:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686801, 369805, 50674, '<td valign="top">Yep, maybe it will be the next one that turns out to be your best:) but I can see that you sort of imagined that people would have their own strings of thoughts and vote according to that.<br/>It should have done better, but c''est la vie on dpc.</td>', 'Yep, maybe it will be the next one that turns out to be your best:) but I can see that you sort of imagined that people would have their own strings of thoughts and vote according to that.It should have done better, but c''est la vie on dpc.', '2006-08-02 03:16:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686805, 369825, 30861, '<td valign="top">I concur with what the Doc says. I''d add to it that the use of a polarizer might help with the rendering of the oblique surfaces on the black arrowhead. But my major reservations about the image lie in the very static composition and the lack of separation of the black arrowhead from the pebbles. I think the 5.5 is a decent score regardless.</td>', 'I concur with what the Doc says. I''d add to it that the use of a polarizer might help with the rendering of the oblique surfaces on the black arrowhead. But my major reservations about the image lie in the very static composition and the lack of separation of the black arrowhead from the pebbles. I think the 5.5 is a decent score regardless.', '2006-08-02 03:18:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686814, 369078, 39880, '<td valign="top">Very Nice.  Doing the team proud!</td>', 'Very Nice.  Doing the team proud!', '2006-08-02 03:22:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686817, 367804, 30861, '<td valign="top">Hey, way to go! A blue ribbon for you! Yippee!</td>', 'Hey, way to go! A blue ribbon for you! Yippee!', '2006-08-02 03:22:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686820, 369838, 30861, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done! Well-deserved ribbon.</td>', 'Very nicely done! Well-deserved ribbon.', '2006-08-02 03:23:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686829, 369649, 30861, '<td valign="top">Sure beat the heck out of your prediction didn''t you? It''s nice to see a full-tone shot take a ribbon in this challenge. Congrats!</td>', 'Sure beat the heck out of your prediction didn''t you? It''s nice to see a full-tone shot take a ribbon in this challenge. Congrats!', '2006-08-02 03:24:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2686844, 369734, 49858, '<td valign="top">Ho hum....  another dice shot. ;) Nice work.</td>', 'Ho hum....  another dice shot. ;) Nice work.', '2006-08-02 03:26:39.000000', NULL, 0),
