(2687866, 369467, 55642, '<td valign="top">Two things immediately leap out at me:<br/> <br/>(1) I would like to see a sharper line at the egg''s edge where it meets the shadow/<br/>(2) Take advantage of the full 640x640 allowance. Not doing so tends to get voted down around here, probably because it indicates a lack of knowledge on how to use your photo editing software? I''m guessing at the reason, but especially on a black and white photo, with very little color data to inflate your file size, there was no reason that a 640x640 couldn''t be saved at 100% using Save for Web.</td>', 'Two things immediately leap out at me: (1) I would like to see a sharper line at the egg''s edge where it meets the shadow/(2) Take advantage of the full 640x640 allowance. Not doing so tends to get voted down around here, probably because it indicates a lack of knowledge on how to use your photo editing software? I''m guessing at the reason, but especially on a black and white photo, with very little color data to inflate your file size, there was no reason that a 640x640 couldn''t be saved at 100% using Save for Web.', '2006-08-02 10:43:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687923, 369838, 27137, '<td valign="top">this was one of my favourites, thought it was well creative as i seen many  pict with that ''funny flower?'' but none like this one</td>', 'this was one of my favourites, thought it was well creative as i seen many  pict with that ''funny flower?'' but none like this one', '2006-08-02 10:57:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2688025, 369374, 35602, '<td valign="top">As promised in the black in white thread last week, I said I would make a comment if I did not during the challenge.  You did a well composed shot, but I think that the material may have kept your score down.  I am sorry to say I gave this one a 4, only because I did comparisons to other shots and felt this one left a bit to be desired.  <br/>Your detail on the washcloth is very good, and your exposure seems just fine.  It is a bit soft in focus, though, and the color did not depict black and white very well.  The best part of the black and white idea is actually the background.  As to the image itself, the color balance appears to be too green, which made the cloth and dish look a bit grimy.</td>', 'As promised in the black in white thread last week, I said I would make a comment if I did not during the challenge.  You did a well composed shot, but I think that the material may have kept your score down.  I am sorry to say I gave this one a 4, only because I did comparisons to other shots and felt this one left a bit to be desired.  Your detail on the washcloth is very good, and your exposure seems just fine.  It is a bit soft in focus, though, and the color did not depict black and white very well.  The best part of the black and white idea is actually the background.  As to the image itself, the color balance appears to be too green, which made the cloth and dish look a bit grimy.', '2006-08-02 11:24:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2688038, 367537, 35602, '<td valign="top">As promised in the black and white scores thread, you e-mailed me wanting a comment after the challenge.  I am afraid I did not score this one very well.  I did not get the point of the blur, and couldn''t figure out why such a blurry image was entered.  It did depict black and white very well.  The lighting seemed to create a nice composition, but I did not get the image at all.  Sorry for the lack of creative sense on my part.</td>', 'As promised in the black and white scores thread, you e-mailed me wanting a comment after the challenge.  I am afraid I did not score this one very well.  I did not get the point of the blur, and couldn''t figure out why such a blurry image was entered.  It did depict black and white very well.  The lighting seemed to create a nice composition, but I did not get the image at all.  Sorry for the lack of creative sense on my part.', '2006-08-02 11:29:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2688059, 367882, 31403, '<td valign="top">No photographers comments????  That''s very disappointing.<br/> <br/>You had it validated and they still beat you up cause they think you cheated - not the brightest bunch.  I believed the validation and gave you the ten - I was just really hoping for some detail on how you did it, maybe a link to the straight from camera too?<br/> <br/>It''s not too late - you can edit your comments!  :-)<br/> <br/></td>', 'No photographers comments????  That''s very disappointing. You had it validated and they still beat you up cause they think you cheated - not the brightest bunch.  I believed the validation and gave you the ten - I was just really hoping for some detail on how you did it, maybe a link to the straight from camera too? It''s not too late - you can edit your comments!  :-) ', '2006-08-02 11:36:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2688081, 369731, 31403, '<td valign="top">147 is just robbery here.  I''ll never get used to how out of step my taste is from the DPC masses.  Shoot two more in a series like this, sell it as a set for kitchens with taste, make $10,000 or so from sales and laugh at the DPC voters with no vision!<br/> <br/>It''s what I do with my "failures" from challenges - I sell them and it makes me feel MUCH better!<br/> <br/>This is good work -</td>', '147 is just robbery here.  I''ll never get used to how out of step my taste is from the DPC masses.  Shoot two more in a series like this, sell it as a set for kitchens with taste, make $10,000 or so from sales and laugh at the DPC voters with no vision! It''s what I do with my "failures" from challenges - I sell them and it makes me feel MUCH better! This is good work -', '2006-08-02 11:46:49.000000', NULL, 0),
