(2694699, 367804, 48739, '<td valign="top">1st i want to say Con gratz on the "Blue" ways to go......this is awesome i can''t wait for the day.... Way to go!</td>', '1st i want to say Con gratz on the "Blue" ways to go......this is awesome i can''t wait for the day.... Way to go!', '2006-08-04 09:08:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2694878, 368495, 47852, '<td valign="top">You posted in the forums that you were looking for comments on how to improve... so here goes.<br/> <br/>When I look at this photo, it doesn''t scream wow to me.  It''s a very contrived set up and for taking so much time to set it up, I''d think you''d have been a bit more careful about making it more precise.  The spacings on the bottom row are uneven, and the dice are slanted at slightly different angles.  With such a symmetrical type of shot, any deviation from an exact setup draws attention to itself I think.<br/> <br/>The lighting was good for what you were trying to achieve, but as others commented, a bit more contrast might have helped.  You also lost some light down in that lower corner, which also draws attention to itself.<br/> <br/>Overall, it''s just kind of a flat shot.  Meets the challenge, was a creative idea as far as technique, but just not executed as well as it could have been.<br/> <br/>Hope this was helpful.</td>', 'You posted in the forums that you were looking for comments on how to improve... so here goes. When I look at this photo, it doesn''t scream wow to me.  It''s a very contrived set up and for taking so much time to set it up, I''d think you''d have been a bit more careful about making it more precise.  The spacings on the bottom row are uneven, and the dice are slanted at slightly different angles.  With such a symmetrical type of shot, any deviation from an exact setup draws attention to itself I think. The lighting was good for what you were trying to achieve, but as others commented, a bit more contrast might have helped.  You also lost some light down in that lower corner, which also draws attention to itself. Overall, it''s just kind of a flat shot.  Meets the challenge, was a creative idea as far as technique, but just not executed as well as it could have been. Hope this was helpful.', '2006-08-04 10:18:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2695183, 368495, 61679, '<td valign="top">Another response from your forum post.  You''ve already heard about the contrast issue so I thought I would add one more item as food for thought.  The way you stacked the chips gives this image a lot of potential for patterns if cropped differently.  As is, the image is all about symmetry, which is slightly off.  If you crop tightly around the dice (About a dice width to the right and left of the end dice) and intersect the chips with the top and bottom borders of the image, the dice become the focal point of the image but the pattern from the chips add a lot of eye appeal.  I often play around with cropping to see how much different looks I can get from an image.</td>', 'Another response from your forum post.  You''ve already heard about the contrast issue so I thought I would add one more item as food for thought.  The way you stacked the chips gives this image a lot of potential for patterns if cropped differently.  As is, the image is all about symmetry, which is slightly off.  If you crop tightly around the dice (About a dice width to the right and left of the end dice) and intersect the chips with the top and bottom borders of the image, the dice become the focal point of the image but the pattern from the chips add a lot of eye appeal.  I often play around with cropping to see how much different looks I can get from an image.', '2006-08-04 12:51:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2695243, 367804, 54431, '<td valign="top">Great job. Congrats on your blue ribbon:-) I love this shot!</td>', 'Great job. Congrats on your blue ribbon:-) I love this shot!', '2006-08-04 13:19:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2695383, 369467, 40718, '<td valign="top">The abstract isn''t bad.  One, if possible, always make sure you have as near 640px on one side as possible.  Lots of people vote lower for smaller pictures just because.  This is in the middle so I don''t know how much it hurt you.  There are tutorials if you are having trouble with getting a full 640px shot at 150kb.<br/> <br/>I do like the geometry of the shot, but perhaps I would have gone for just a tiny bit more definition at the upper edges of the egg.  On my monitor (which is a laptop and so has some limitations) the egg is totally lost at the top and my eye doesn''t quite like that as much.<br/> <br/>Also just be aware that abstracts tend to do poorly at DPC outside of an actual abstract challenge.  That shouldn''t stop you, but it just helps answer the question of why your score was where it is.</td>', 'The abstract isn''t bad.  One, if possible, always make sure you have as near 640px on one side as possible.  Lots of people vote lower for smaller pictures just because.  This is in the middle so I don''t know how much it hurt you.  There are tutorials if you are having trouble with getting a full 640px shot at 150kb. I do like the geometry of the shot, but perhaps I would have gone for just a tiny bit more definition at the upper edges of the egg.  On my monitor (which is a laptop and so has some limitations) the egg is totally lost at the top and my eye doesn''t quite like that as much. Also just be aware that abstracts tend to do poorly at DPC outside of an actual abstract challenge.  That shouldn''t stop you, but it just helps answer the question of why your score was where it is.', '2006-08-04 14:18:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2695415, 369374, 40718, '<td valign="top">Well, you chose the right challenge as I think this would have done even worse in color on color.  A few issues.  First is subject matter.  I think the average person looked at this and just asked "huh?".  It doesn''t seem to represent something in real life.  The title indicates it is "after supper", but we have two full glasses of water, a clean napkin, and a clean plate.  I do like your attempt at "creating" something (I like to do that myself), but in this case I think it just was something that didn''t resonate with the voter.<br/> <br/>Technically  the shot could have used a little more contrast (especially the blacks).  It is quite centered compositionally which lends even more of a static feel which may not be helpful.  The picture also looks somewhat soft.  Perhaps that was on purpose, but a bit of USM could have helped there.  I''m sure the despeckle and dust and scratches removed some detail as well.<br/> <br/>Keep working at things.  I see you are making an effort to come up with something original.  That''s always good.</td>', 'Well, you chose the right challenge as I think this would have done even worse in color on color.  A few issues.  First is subject matter.  I think the average person looked at this and just asked "huh?".  It doesn''t seem to represent something in real life.  The title indicates it is "after supper", but we have two full glasses of water, a clean napkin, and a clean plate.  I do like your attempt at "creating" something (I like to do that myself), but in this case I think it just was something that didn''t resonate with the voter. Technically  the shot could have used a little more contrast (especially the blacks).  It is quite centered compositionally which lends even more of a static feel which may not be helpful.  The picture also looks somewhat soft.  Perhaps that was on purpose, but a bit of USM could have helped there.  I''m sure the despeckle and dust and scratches removed some detail as well. Keep working at things.  I see you are making an effort to come up with something original.  That''s always good.', '2006-08-04 14:29:13.000000', NULL, 0),
