(2713922, 367804, 21601, '<td valign="top">Great photo<br/> <br/>reminds me of this song.<br/> <br/>San Francisco Mabel Joy<br/> <br/>His Daddy was a simple man, just a red dirt Georgia farmer<br/>And his Momma spent her young life havin kids and balin hay<br/>He had fifteen years and an ache inside to wander<br/>So he hopped a freight in Waycross and wound up in L.A.<br/> <br/>Lord, the cold nights had no pity on a Waycross, Georgia farm boy<br/>Most days he went hungry, then the summer came<br/>He met a girl known on the strip as San Franciscos Mabel Joy<br/>Destitutions child born of an L.A. street called Shame<br/> <br/>Growin up came quietly in the arms of Mabel Joy<br/>Laughter found their mornings brought meaning to his life<br/>Yes, the night before she left sleep came and left that Waycross, Georgia boy<br/>With dreams of Georgia cotton and a California wife<br/> <br/>Sunday morning found him standin neath the red light at her door<br/>When a right cross sent him reelin, put him face down on the floor<br/>In place of Mabel Joy he found a merchant mad marine<br/>Who growled, Your Georgia neck is red but sonny, youre still green<br/> <br/>He turned twenty-one in a gray rock fedral prison<br/>The old judge had no mercy for a Waycross, Georgia boy<br/>Starin at those four gray walls in silence he would listen<br/>To that midnight freight he knew would take him back to Mabel Joy<br/> <br/>Sunday mornin found him standin neath the red light at her door<br/>With a bullet in his side, he cried, Have you seen Mabel Joy?<br/>Stunned and shaken someone said, Why, shes not here no more<br/>She left this house four years today, they say shes lookin for some Gergia farm boy<br/> <br/>Words and Music by Mickey Newbury<br/></td>', 'Great photo reminds me of this song. San Francisco Mabel Joy His Daddy was a simple man, just a red dirt Georgia farmerAnd his Momma spent her young life havin kids and balin hayHe had fifteen years and an ache inside to wanderSo he hopped a freight in Waycross and wound up in L.A. Lord, the cold nights had no pity on a Waycross, Georgia farm boyMost days he went hungry, then the summer cameHe met a girl known on the strip as San Franciscos Mabel JoyDestitutions child born of an L.A. street called Shame Growin up came quietly in the arms of Mabel JoyLaughter found their mornings brought meaning to his lifeYes, the night before she left sleep came and left that Waycross, Georgia boyWith dreams of Georgia cotton and a California wife Sunday morning found him standin neath the red light at her doorWhen a right cross sent him reelin, put him face down on the floorIn place of Mabel Joy he found a merchant mad marineWho growled, Your Georgia neck is red but sonny, youre still green He turned twenty-one in a gray rock fedral prisonThe old judge had no mercy for a Waycross, Georgia boyStarin at those four gray walls in silence he would listenTo that midnight freight he knew would take him back to Mabel Joy Sunday mornin found him standin neath the red light at her doorWith a bullet in his side, he cried, Have you seen Mabel Joy?Stunned and shaken someone said, Why, shes not here no moreShe left this house four years today, they say shes lookin for some Gergia farm boy Words and Music by Mickey Newbury', '2006-08-10 08:35:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2715719, 369228, 14614, '<td valign="top">oooo -- this one get slammed by the voters... not too sure why?? ( perhaps lack of detail in the silhouettes?) it''s crispy crisp in focus and just typical-you in the everyday scene very well framed.  I like the natural frame-balance of the solid gray/black bands.  I agree with the other commenter on just the pop of yellow that adds so much.  Didn''t vote but would have scored this one high... unique and soo "meets the challenge"</td>', 'oooo -- this one get slammed by the voters... not too sure why?? ( perhaps lack of detail in the silhouettes?) it''s crispy crisp in focus and just typical-you in the everyday scene very well framed.  I like the natural frame-balance of the solid gray/black bands.  I agree with the other commenter on just the pop of yellow that adds so much.  Didn''t vote but would have scored this one high... unique and soo "meets the challenge"', '2006-08-10 19:58:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2720818, 369141, 61679, '<td valign="top">Jeanne,<br/> <br/>I like the composition of this image and I wouldn''t change a thing.  On the technical side, the white balance is a little off, which is casting a yellow hue on the milk.  This image would also benefit from a bit more contrast and some noise reduction.<br/> <br/>This image was a little hard to play with from the image posted in the challenge but I gave it a try anyways.<br/> <br/>Post Processign Steps.<br/> <br/>- Color Balance Layer: Reduce Yellow in both the midtone and highlights (Midtone settings 0-0-21 Highlight settings 0-0-25).  The 21 &amp; 25 are setting for the amount of yellow reduction on the yellow-blue adjustment bar.<br/>- Levels Layer: Input Settings 20-1-255 (This increases contrast)<br/>- Noise Reduction<br/>- USM (Radius 1, Strength 100, Clipping 5)<br/> <br/><a href="//static.flickr.com/89/213347760_7b2f1bc295_o.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//static.flickr.com/89/213347760_7b2f1bc295_t.jpg'', strrpos(''//static.flickr.com/89/213347760_7b2f1bc295_t.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//static.flickr.com/89/213347760_7b2f1bc295_t.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Jeanne, I like the composition of this image and I wouldn''t change a thing.  On the technical side, the white balance is a little off, which is casting a yellow hue on the milk.  This image would also benefit from a bit more contrast and some noise reduction. This image was a little hard to play with from the image posted in the challenge but I gave it a try anyways. Post Processign Steps. - Color Balance Layer: Reduce Yellow in both the midtone and highlights (Midtone settings 0-0-21 Highlight settings 0-0-25).  The 21 & 25 are setting for the amount of yellow reduction on the yellow-blue adjustment bar.- Levels Layer: Input Settings 20-1-255 (This increases contrast)- Noise Reduction- USM (Radius 1, Strength 100, Clipping 5)   Tim', '2006-08-12 15:51:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2721121, 369856, 15711, '<td valign="top">OMG!!!!  How on earth did I miss this?  I love the subtle quality. It is wonderful. It has intrigue because you have to study it.  I love photos like that.  What an eye for detail!</td>', 'OMG!!!!  How on earth did I miss this?  I love the subtle quality. It is wonderful. It has intrigue because you have to study it.  I love photos like that.  What an eye for detail!', '2006-08-12 19:13:29.000000', NULL, 0),
